        "category": "stale_orientation_after_self_edit",
        "summary": "The final implementation turn ran its orientation reseal before its last edit rather than after, leaving the receipt stale. With both correction rounds spent, the review packet is refused and a completed rewrite that passes every acceptance check cannot be reviewed. Third occurrence of this exact mechanism, and the third partial it has caused.",
        "evidence": "The turn is recorded incomplete with error beginning 'stale bob orientation', yet its outputs are all present and correct: README.md 260 to 96 lines, VALIDATION_RESULTS.md 781 to a 16-line pointer, both new per-scheme reports at 602 and 452 lines, every file returning 0 for grep -c '1DMIX-', no cross-file scheme references anywhere, audit.py PASS. workflow_records.py review-packet refuses a packet whose latest implementation attempt is unresolved, and reserve refuses correction_round 3 against a limit of 2 regardless of which identity is dispatched.",
        "minutes_lost": 15
      },
      {
        "category": "short_turn_strategy_avoided_breach",
        "summary": "Recorded here because the schema has no success channel: splitting the rewrite into three short focused turns instead of one long turn kept every turn well under the 12-dollar per-turn cap that breached 1DMIX-054, and produced durable files at each step. This is the direct mitigation for the previous iteration's unrecoverable failure and it worked.",
        "evidence": "Three turns at $4.39, $5.00 and $7.99, total $17.39 against a $60 scope with no breach, compared with 1DMIX-054's single turn at $12.735 which breached a $12 cap and made that scope permanently undispatchable. Each turn also landed complete files rather than leaving work in an unwritten buffer, so no output was lost when the third turn was recorded incomplete.",
